WHAT IS TARGET SCOPING??

1. process of defining exactly what systems, networks or applications you are allowed to test
PS: Only for the one that is authorized only

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Common types of targets
-- during reconn, targets are usually defined in 1 or more of the following ways

Domain-Based Targets
Examples: exampl.com, testsite.local
a domain based scope may include:
- the primary domain
- subdomain 

IP Based Target
- a single ip address
- a network range
* commonly in internal or lab based env or cloud based

Application-based targets
- a specific web app
- a login portal / api endpoint
* focus on application/endpoint, not entire server

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In-Scope
assest you are allowed to 
- collect info from
- scan
-enumerate

Out-scope 
assest you must not interact with
- third part services
- external domain not listed in scope
- systems owned by another org
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHY SCOPING  MATTERS

its about collecting useful info, not collect all info
- without proper scoping:
-- you may scan irrelevant hosts
-- you may miss the actual tagret
-- your results become noisy and confusing

- a well defined scope keeps your reconn
-- focues
-- efficient
-- relevant to later stages

